><published>2026-11-25T18:52:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/peter-magyar-meets-volodymyr-zelenskyy-hungary-and-ukraine-make-a-fresh-start-after-the-icy-relation/a-80054175--5597adb6deec.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/peter-magyar-meets-volodymyr-zelenskyy-hungary-and-ukraine-make-a-fresh-start-after-the-icy-relations-of-the-viktor-orban-era/a-80054175?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">After years of frosty and hostile relations under Hungary's Kremlin-friendly former PM Viktor Orban, his successor, Peter Magyar, and Ukrainian President Volodymyr Zelenskyy seek to reset their countries' ties.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Spain: Canary Islands witness 1-day migration record</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:cdd6c9113d0ad6beeb5d36bb0d2e1f809cf80545ad002ca77a1b9256a920cd90</id><updated>2026-11-26T08:38:13Z</updated><published>2026-11-25T18:00:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/spain-canary-islands-witness-1-day-migration-record/a-80052770--8a7d7af8fd05.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/spain-canary-islands-witness-1-day-migration-record/a-80052770?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The arrival of over 2,000 migrants to the islands comes as Spain holds elections this weekend. The president of the Canary Islands said the archipelago is facing "unprecedented migration pressure."</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>€561 Billion and Still Not Enough: Germany's 2027 Budget Exposes a Coalition on the Brink</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2d01d8d13d5d3b8724fee726be5128cebe5741c502592cb23398fa3115eadf4a</id><updated>2026-11-26T08:38:13Z</updated><published>2026-11-25T16:06:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/561-billion-and-still-not-enough-germany-s-2027-budget-exposes-a-coalition-on-the-brink/a-80052664--c8b0f8b87743.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/€561-billion-and-still-not-enough-germany-s-2027-budget-exposes-a-coalition-on-the-brink/a-80052664?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The budget for 2027 has reached new highs, and pension funds, defense spending and a weak economy are increasing the pressure. At the same time, tensions are mounting within the government.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>US Army detonates unstable lead-based explosives in Iowa</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:389bd52121c8cad974d89d95fd1536962b3395da8468b7a2ac963857893de8b0</id><updated>2026-11-26T08:38:13Z</updated><published>2026-11-25T15:38:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/us-army-detonates-unstable-lead-based-explosives-in-iowa/a-80043319--c4804e3d6ed1.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/us-army-detonates-unstable-lead-based-explosives-in-iowa/a-80043319?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The US Army says a controlled blast is the safest way to deal with explosive chemicals that began crystallizing in storage. US President Donald Trump said "mitigation efforts have far exceeded expectations."</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>EU must set out a new timeline for cage-free farming, court rules</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:82e4a5daf318ce846bb799ed1d71b407f05754dc56c72cb09986c78b2970f683</id><updated>2026-11-26T08:38:13Z</updated><published>2026-11-25T15:36:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/eu-must-set-out-a-new-timeline-for-cage-free-farming-court-rules/a-80051729--5055be48cf6e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/eu-must-set-out-a-new-timeline-for-cage-free-farming-court-rules/a-80051729?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">European General Court ruled that the European Commission has failed to set out a timeline after pledging to end caged farming by the end of 2023.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Nigeria's upcoming election marred by rising AI disinformation</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:99720c16d87f7f7b55dffb27caee3a221c65ac53403a21aad71e10a67c9c57eb</id><updated>2026-11-26T08:38:13Z</updated><published>2026-11-25T15:28:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/nigeria-s-upcoming-election-marred-by-rising-ai-disinformation/a-79946897--e1618bd315dd.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/nigeria-s-upcoming-election-marred-by-rising-ai-disinformation/a-79946897?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">As Nigeria inches closer to the 2027 polls, the use of artificial intelligence in the electoral process has prompted questions about integrity and institutional readiness. Can Nigerians trust their democratic processes?</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Ukraine: Poland to set up no-fly zone near Ukraine border</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:087c792a55348e22c24858358b9f5e71e930e88f2eaf2b2ab38f7872a7fd4392</id><updated>2026-11-26T08:38:13Z</updated><published>2026-11-25T14:59:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/ukraine-poland-to-set-up-no-fly-zone-near-ukraine-border/live-80047122--a9b171e10de2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/ukraine-poland-to-set-up-no-fly-zone-near-ukraine-border/live-80047122?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Poland urged NATO allies to be vigilant at their borders after repeated Russian airspace incursions. Allies have also offered different opinions on Kyiv attacking Russian ships in Libya.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>US plans new tariffs on EU, China and 12 others</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:01a6350ccd5d9a0ef870092fcf1cf601540fe1b48708e9d80443033765bf3669</id><updated>2026-11-26T08:38:13Z</updated><published>2026-11-25T14:54:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/us-plans-new-tariffs-on-eu-china-and-12-others/a-80050872--4aaf71a33ac8.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/us-plans-new-tariffs-on-eu-china-and-12-others/a-80050872?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The Trump administration is planning new import duties of up to 20% to counter excessive manufacturing abroad. The measures could put further pressure on US consumers already struggling with high living costs.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>German firms eye Africa as global trade shocks hit traditional markets</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:cc8cb60cdb8c9bd0d4e4617a860cff3f359167a5a663c2a933eeb8c476d5b46e</id><updated>2026-11-26T08:38:13Z</updated><published>2026-11-25T14:38:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/german-firms-eye-africa-as-global-trade-shocks-hit-traditional-markets/a-80047671--b64160bb0ab9.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/german-firms-eye-africa-as-global-trade-shocks-hit-traditional-markets/a-80047671?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">German businesses are optimistic about Africa, but Berlin's cautious approach to risk is holding them back from cashing in on the opportunities that their competitors from countries like the UAE and Turkey are seizing.</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>Ice hockey prospect Max Calce follows Leon Draisaitl's path, leaving Mannheim for Canada</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7d0fb93436a709cb39b3996518f41c89014d2e61d7ed4efc57b4eb25e6683f09</id><updated>2026-11-26T08:38:13Z</updated><published>2026-11-25T13:28:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/ice-hockey-prospect-max-calce-follows-leon-draisaitl-s-path-leaving-mannheim-for-canada/a-80049458--4ca1ab8cf6e4.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/ice-hockey-prospect-max-calce-follows-leon-draisaitl-s-path-leaving-mannheim-for-canada/a-80049458?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The player widely seen as Germany's biggest ice hockey talent to come along in years is leaving the country's top professional league for Canada – changing tracks in his bid to make it to the NHL.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Climate loss and damage fund exists, but the money doesn't</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1f47708ad8b33edec731d66da0dc12e43eec212061edda0d42cbd6d01f3a0dad</id><updated>2026-11-26T08:38:13Z</updated><published>2026-11-25T09:49:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/climate-loss-and-damage-fund-exists-but-the-money-doesn-t/a-80035620--dbacc66829c5.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/climate-loss-and-damage-fund-exists-but-the-money-doesn-t/a-80035620?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Climate-vulnerable countries fought for years to create a loss and damage fund. Four years on, demand far outstrips funding, pledges are scarce, and disaster-hit nations are still waiting for support.</summary><category term="Environment" /></entry><entry><title>Germany's women's football team take stand against domestic violence</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8cddec1549f1eccd797a1670be6e88a8384f86ecd7f9ba59731f67d4a83c4f2c</id><updated>2026-11-26T08:38:13Z</updated><published>2026-11-25T09:30:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-s-women-s-football-team-take-stand-against-domestic-violence/a-70907974--84aba926a54f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-s-women-s-football-team-take-stand-against-domestic-violence/a-70907974?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Germany's women's football team are to wear UN Women badges in games against Argentina and Peru, as domestic violence hits a record high in Germany.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>German auto workers on back foot as costs, competition bite</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ca147bd776998e8922483601aa1d4115bb17aeccfe83a36dcf7ef0942d8a884e</id><updated>2026-11-26T08:38:13Z</updated><published>2026-11-25T08:51:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/german-auto-workers-on-back-foot-as-costs-competition-bite/a-80036111--50a0a19d14b3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/german-auto-workers-on-back-foot-as-costs-competition-bite/a-80036111?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">German auto workers profited during the industry's boom years, but are now increasingly being asked to trade past gains for future job security.</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>Domestic violence soars to record high in Germany</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:093960e94d3ade01a6c2e89797df4ed0eb71337ae3639048cbf2dc7802f0a5df</id><updated>2026-11-26T08:38:13Z</updated><published>2026-11-25T06:57:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/domestic-violence-soars-to-record-high-in-germany/a-80041678--cb6cf80357ec.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/domestic-violence-soars-to-record-high-in-germany/a-80041678?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Every three days in Germany, a man kills his wife or ex-partner. Every 10 minutes, the police record a sexual offense against a woman. "A shocking finding," according to Justice Minister Stefanie Hubig.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>Ukraine's bid for NATO membership and more air defense remains controversial</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ddf73536425e910ee2c0e16f447d924c4f365fc0211b7c82c88e91119a7a7cb3</id><updated>2026-11-26T08:38:13Z</updated><published>2026-11-24T16:18:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/ukraine-s-bid-for-nato-membership-and-more-air-defense-remains-controversial/a-80029852--1abf02560b4b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/ukraine-s-bid-for-nato-membership-and-more-air-defense-remains-controversial/a-80029852?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Ukrainian President Volodymyr Zelenskyy is calling for the rapid acceptance of his country into NATO. However, the necessary unanimity for this is lacking, as shown during the NATO Parliamentary Assembly in Berlin.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>EU enlargement: Why do some EU member states use their vetoes to block the accession of certain candidate countries?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:92803055dd208b9b8d88aac25bb4b40f7d9d0c4e5cb36efbe1dab64bdff4ed8b</id><updated>2026-11-26T08:38:13Z</updated><published>2026-11-24T14:49:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/eu-enlargement-why-do-some-eu-member-states-use-their-vetoes-to-block-the-accession-of-certain-candi/a-80034401--27cd622204d3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/eu-enlargement-why-do-some-eu-member-states-use-their-vetoes-to-block-the-accession-of-certain-candidate-countries/a-80034401?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Individual EU member states use their veto powers to block candidate countries in the accession process — often for reasons of domestic politics. DW takes a look at some cases and examines what's behind them.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>CAS reinstates Senegal as 2025 AFCON champions</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:fc29d47c7e8d189897203880e4a9a4f78ce7af5964a55a3f09d4b4f5aad596c0</id><updated>2026-11-26T08:38:13Z</updated><published>2026-11-24T14:42:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/cas-reinstates-senegal-as-2025-afcon-champions/a-80021027--561a21777065.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/cas-reinstates-senegal-as-2025-afcon-champions/a-80021027?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The Court of Arbitration for Sport has reinstated Senegal as 2025 AFCON champions, overturning a CAF decision that stripped them of the title. Morocco, previously declared winners, are confirmed runners-up.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Bombed factories, billion-dollar opportunity: Why German companies are staying in Ukraine</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:50624c7100b2ccec37f261455d5e289606f6946c6494a8e22dc93803e2f71202</id><updated>2026-11-26T08:38:13Z</updated><published>2026-11-24T11:00:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/bombed-factories-billion-dollar-opportunity-why-german-companies-are-staying-in-ukraine/a-80030201--13f674deb921.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/bombed-factories-billion-dollar-opportunity-why-german-companies-are-staying-in-ukraine/a-80030201?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">German companies remain committed to Ukraine despite million-dollar losses, an unreliable energy supply and a shortage of skilled workers. They are betting on new markets and long-term growth.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>How cautious investors are struggling to avoid the AI bubble</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4c02879edf2de21f28acf4c23db9aa8b344110a0ca76963df3a1f55350d05655</id><updated>2026-11-26T08:38:13Z</updated><published>2026-11-24T10:59:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/how-cautious-investors-are-struggling-to-avoid-the-ai-bubble/a-80016412--863307befc9b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/how-cautious-investors-are-struggling-to-avoid-the-ai-bubble/a-80016412?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">From Nvidia to Coreweave, AI and tech stocks have swung sharply in recent months. Some investors still see plenty of room to run, while others are trying to diversify — and finding it harder than expected.</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>German directors' doc on stolen film wins International Emmy Award</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:789ad99fe845f8d51f4456a456f02133ec35b8a3326c44d239efd34afc8b63ad</id><updated>2026-11-26T08:38:13Z</updated><published>2026-11-24T09:41:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/german-directors-doc-on-stolen-film-wins-international-emmy-award/a-76103455--80792ca0c998.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/german-directors-doc-on-stolen-film-wins-international-emmy-award/a-76103455?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Two German film students confronted the American who won festival prizes with their animated movie. "The Talented Mr. F," their documentary on their fight against plagiarism, is now in the spotlight.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>What happens if a nuclear weapon explodes in space?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0dfb4406cfa5b103e1eae233f494fb75d11d2e0ea3017e6ffd90acdc8c7a25d4</id><updated>2026-11-26T08:38:13Z</updated><published>2026-11-24T08:34:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/what-happens-if-a-nuclear-weapon-explodes-in-space/a-80025827--a6201a0063e7.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/what-happens-if-a-nuclear-weapon-explodes-in-space/a-80025827?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Earth's atmosphere offers protection from a nuclear blast in space, but satellites are more exposed. We explain how radiation could damage them, why the effects can linger and what protection is possible.</summary><category term="Science" /></entry><entry><title>Weapons, war and wavering trust: Germans want to see more restraint in foreign policy</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c080fe989051126614d0ac4e040d48ce9020a663ec37cd95005df5d8b824c4fa</id><updated>2026-11-26T08:38:13Z</updated><published>2026-11-24T05:59:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/weapons-war-and-wavering-trust-germans-want-to-see-more-restraint-in-foreign-policy/a-80026254--66b3f174435c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/weapons-war-and-wavering-trust-germans-want-to-see-more-restraint-in-foreign-policy/a-80026254?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">According to a study by the Körber Foundation, a growing number of Germans now oppose providing military aid to Ukraine. The majority also believes that Germany should take a neutral position between the US and China.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>US and UK to host Women's World Cups in 2031 and 2035</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d213e4c246ff3eaebeef3fb8b9a5a67bbe46f7e526b0dc06194e028c5bccdee2</id><updated>2026-11-26T08:38:13Z</updated><published>2026-11-23T16:19:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/us-and-uk-to-host-women-s-world-cups-in-2031-and-2035/a-80023786--81630f151694.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/us-and-uk-to-host-women-s-world-cups-in-2031-and-2035/a-80023786?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">FIFA has confirmed the United States, Mexico, Costa Rica and Jamaica will host the 2031 Women's World Cup — the first to feature 48 teams. The UK will stage the 2035 edition, its first World Cup since 1966.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Gukesh to defend chess crown against rising star Sindarov</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e6736fca4ec4abe45aa56d3b5ba42a78bbd76c423a7157516c8d1f10f3135644</id><updated>2026-11-26T08:38:13Z</updated><published>2026-11-23T15:31:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/gukesh-to-defend-chess-crown-against-rising-star-sindarov/a-80021806--07e5204aa07f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/gukesh-to-defend-chess-crown-against-rising-star-sindarov/a-80021806?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">As the World Chess championship gets underway, it's no coincidence that the titleholder, Gukesh Dommaraju, and his challenger, Jakhovir Sindarov, are both from Asia.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Nvidia reinstates former CEO Jensen Huang despite China espionage scandal</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9e2eb7d21502ba380a77c0cb357a42168a30771671c0567191767f73cc3650c1</id><updated>2026-11-26T08:38:13Z</updated><published>2026-11-23T14:18:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/nvidia-reinstates-former-ceo-jensen-huang-despite-china-espionage-scandal/a-80021926--88659c21678b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/nvidia-reinstates-former-ceo-jensen-huang-despite-china-espionage-scandal/a-80021926?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Nvidia's board voted unanimously to bring back the disgraced CEO, who resigned this month amid news of his affairs. He's suspected of having had a relationship with a Chinese intelligence asset.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>North Macedonia remains stalled on its EU path after 21 years as a candidate</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:254c08a72685dc66438bf60f41bacae2e846e64af054f8cc228059ef02343e56</id><updated>2026-11-26T08:38:13Z</updated><published>2026-11-23T13:46:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/north-macedonia-remains-stalled-on-its-eu-path-after-21-years-as-a-candidate/a-80020841--291e539f1390.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/north-macedonia-remains-stalled-on-its-eu-path-after-21-years-as-a-candidate/a-80020841?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">EU enlargement has regained momentum, with Montenegro and Albania moving closer to membership. But North Macedonia, a candidate since 2005, remains stalled by a politically difficult dispute involving Bulgaria.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Uganda minister at COP31: 'We need a just transition'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:75e34f38f9396b2e2f8500823819af4aa67008c44f71bb559c01ce95534c8201</id><updated>2026-11-26T08:38:13Z</updated><published>2026-11-23T13:18:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/uganda-minister-at-cop31-we-need-a-just-transition/a-79997209--312e033bb073.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/uganda-minister-at-cop31-we-need-a-just-transition/a-79997209?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Funding from wealthy countries to help deal with the impacts of climate change hasn't materialized, says Uganda's environment minister. The East African country is hoping oil and carbon credits will help boost finances.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>COP deadlock prompts calls for a reset of climate diplomacy</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6b4fde327c0bffb8435dd36fb877d45956aae6f87c6f5d5d2d31549a32bef3c7</id><updated>2026-11-26T08:38:13Z</updated><published>2026-11-23T13:03:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/cop-deadlock-prompts-calls-for-a-reset-of-climate-diplomacy/a-80020494--3b4f8cad49dc.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/cop-deadlock-prompts-calls-for-a-reset-of-climate-diplomacy/a-80020494?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">COP31 has been branded a failure after countries couldn't reach a final agreement, divided over a reference to "fossil fuels." But was the decision to walk away from a watered-down text actually a show of strength?</summary><category term="Environment" /></entry><entry><title>German police respond to multiple school bomb threats</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d380ef0c69ce36676f88fd970e497572996e790d91e94a146c4c7eac9146145c</id><updated>2026-11-26T08:38:13Z</updated><published>2026-11-23T11:01:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/german-police-respond-to-multiple-school-bomb-threats/a-80018842--56ba1301d92a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/german-police-respond-to-multiple-school-bomb-threats/a-80018842?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Police in Germany are responding to bomb threats against a series of schools, but say that at present they don't believe them to be credible. Danish authorities are reporting a similar series of apparent hoaxes.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>'I've lost her forever' — Why German voice actors are refusing to sign Netflix's AI contract</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:12f54b4095e11988137f4f2b230ab73218c62f1666a299534759844088e34d3d</id><updated>2026-11-26T08:38:13Z</updated><published>2026-11-23T10:58:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/i-ve-lost-her-forever-why-german-voice-actors-are-refusing-to-sign-netflix-s-ai-contract/a-80004381--da3277b6e37b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/i-ve-lost-her-forever-why-german-voice-actors-are-refusing-to-sign-netflix-s-ai-contract/a-80004381?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">For decades, Germans have known Hollywood's biggest stars through the same familiar voices. Now an AI clause in Netflix contracts is splitting the industry over whether it protects performers or exposes them.</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>Budget cuts threaten Germany's fight against antisemitism and racism</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8e1f0cd37982731e13e73abaadf4c8d755083834b7e4a8515f7cd3d2471caa1e</id><updated>2026-11-26T08:38:13Z</updated><published>2026-11-23T10:55:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/budget-cuts-threaten-germany-s-fight-against-antisemitism-and-racism/a-80018644--fcf379d5b1d2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/budget-cuts-threaten-germany-s-fight-against-antisemitism-and-racism/a-80018644?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Numerous grassroots initiatives in Germany are facing funding cuts. Affected organizations are sounding the alarm, pointing to growing challenges posed by far-right extremism.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>Rembrandt's 'The Night Watch' is more alive than you'd expect</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2396e1cba8801948b568adcb9f6ccb8d6b5c28f6b6c6cc233fed10e8d0a05b7a</id><updated>2026-11-26T08:38:13Z</updated><published>2026-11-23T10:33:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/rembrandt-s-the-night-watch-is-more-alive-than-you-d-expect/a-79972540--0d1ff511f0b9.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/rembrandt-s-the-night-watch-is-more-alive-than-you-d-expect/a-79972540?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A new project and exhibition, "The Night Watch Lives," lifts the veil on the hidden world of microbes covering one of the most famous paintings of the Dutch Golden Age.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>Germany's Early Start Pension: Can child investment accounts help?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c869fc12c6eda89363fc624c13d3163f39bc2d7cc0730791f3d7204f9d8a1577</id><updated>2026-11-26T08:38:13Z</updated><published>2026-11-23T09:26:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-s-early-start-pension-can-child-investment-accounts-help/a-79852185--25ffc2424261.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-s-early-start-pension-can-child-investment-accounts-help/a-79852185?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Germany plans to pay €10 a month into investment accounts for children to encourage long-term retirement saving. Economists say the measure may help build wealth but won't solve the country's pension funding challenge.</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>Germany news: Metalworkers go on strike as pay dispute heats up</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:bed514248cb5150da7f4a05577f283bf859fb8ede53ee7af88f153cc2e7939e8</id><updated>2026-11-26T08:38:13Z</updated><published>2026-11-23T07:11:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-news-metalworkers-go-on-strike-as-pay-dispute-heats-up/live-80015633--a1790c046188.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-news-metalworkers-go-on-strike-as-pay-dispute-heats-up/live-80015633?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Germany's biggest union is calling for more strikes over heated pay disputes with car makers like Mercedes and shipyards among the companies impacted. Meanwhile, a Berlin hospital fire leaves many injured.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>Rule-breaking is contagious — and good examples barely help</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:158084693ec0388d790e43a1e0438f0ba06ea6fc8f86dcc3599ed2a4cfeedc5a</id><updated>2026-11-26T08:38:13Z</updated><published>2026-11-23T06:33:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/rule-breaking-is-contagious-and-good-examples-barely-help/a-79980025--098488c374ac.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/rule-breaking-is-contagious-and-good-examples-barely-help/a-79980025?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Seeing someone break a rule makes people more likely to break it too, a new study finds, especially when the rule-breaker is on their side politically. Watching others behave well barely made a difference.</summary><category term="Science" /></entry><entry><title>COP31 climate talks end without consensus on how to fund vulnerable countries or move the world away from coal, oil and gas use</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2b41dc6d71600421f62e5dee5bd35aa2a73dc2171c59de8707a8735f8282f491</id><updated>2026-11-26T08:38:13Z</upd