asylum seekers to Rwanda. In other news, business start-ups in Germany are on track to reach the highest level since 2015.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>France's Philippe Diallo to challenge Infantino for FIFA presidency</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2871b69e7852dd24ef6eebf7cd00448e939ba49c3ef1af11be0f83f7fa1e529d</id><updated>2026-11-26T08:38:13Z</updated><published>2026-11-16T20:24:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/france-s-philippe-diallo-to-challenge-infantino-for-fifa-presidency/a-79962843--6fe08ae5c0bf.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/france-s-philippe-diallo-to-challenge-infantino-for-fifa-presidency/a-79962843?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Philippe Diallo is the second candidate to stand against incumbent Gianni Infantino. He is backed by European football's governing body UEFA, known to be critical of Infantino.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>NASA's Voyager 1 reaches a light-day away from Earth</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6a9fd2146fcf45ed39a88d60891792fc7cd5bc7668bab2be2dda3b9564b624bc</id><updated>2026-11-26T08:38:13Z</updated><published>2026-11-16T17:24:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/nasa-s-voyager-1-reaches-a-light-day-away-from-earth/a-79961817--190e9087abf2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/nasa-s-voyager-1-reaches-a-light-day-away-from-earth/a-79961817?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">When just saying 'hello' takes a two-day round trip, you're a light-day, or 26 billion kilometers, from Earth. Only one human-made object has ever traveled that far — and its journey into interstellar space continues.</summary><category term="Science" /></entry><entry><title>What has changed in James Bond films over the decades</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:49ad6c3636efa68b599901590663bdb97480647ea647f8fe4bb1bfbc4d0890f1</id><updated>2026-11-26T08:38:13Z</updated><published>2026-11-16T17:07:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/what-has-changed-in-james-bond-films-over-the-decades/a-63332001--7d894a9cd4fe.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/what-has-changed-in-james-bond-films-over-the-decades/a-63332001?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">In 1962, a martini-drinking womanizer saved the world for the first time in "Dr. No." As Robert Pattinson takes on the role of 007, here's how the films evolved.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>The AfD and neo-Nazi networks: How close are the connections?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ba719097a841d6ad90b1c24d0dc23522ef6104abe84740912567cd0858d83564</id><updated>2026-11-26T08:38:13Z</updated><published>2026-11-16T16:23:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/the-afd-and-neo-nazi-networks-how-close-are-the-connections/a-79961920--fb16f5d74381.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/the-afd-and-neo-nazi-networks-how-close-are-the-connections/a-79961920?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The Alternative for Germany party (AfD) has become a focal point for the far right. Many of its members and staff have ties to ethnonationalist or neo-Nazi organizations.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>COP31 draft deal calls for 'immediate' shift away from fossil fuels</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:77c30bb9416e175255f3f09e706b2dd5c0b3780abaf9e6a3643fe05052f562d8</id><updated>2026-11-26T08:38:13Z</updated><published>2026-11-16T14:05:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/cop31-draft-deal-calls-for-immediate-shift-away-from-fossil-fuels/a-79960705--2a7f1bfc2c85.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/cop31-draft-deal-calls-for-immediate-shift-away-from-fossil-fuels/a-79960705?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The preliminary agreement at UN climate talks in Turkey calls for a rapid reduction of planet-warming emissions and at least $120 billion to help countries adapt to climate change.</summary><category term="Environment" /></entry><entry><title>Klopp wants Infantino out as FIFA candidate deadline looms</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4ebf65beef74c46a0e2cba7b30bf1b9f7e12431c7fcfa4627083004bf5f3aa46</id><updated>2026-11-26T08:38:13Z</updated><published>2026-11-16T11:59:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/klopp-wants-infantino-out-as-fifa-candidate-deadline-looms/a-79958229--458d3356c9f8.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/klopp-wants-infantino-out-as-fifa-candidate-deadline-looms/a-79958229?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Germany coach Jürgen Klopp has joined the chorus of football figures critical of FIFA President Gianni Infantino. But with time running out, there are few who seem willing to run against him.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Germany news: Merz, Söder aim to revisit electricity tax cut</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:02329d5db47c92c14d1795feaec484ce9c00a92eba968149637523e20736867f</id><updated>2026-11-26T08:38:13Z</updated><published>2026-11-16T08:37:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-news-merz-s_der-aim-to-revisit-electricity-tax-cut/live-79954869--6bc156ed2286.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-news-merz-söder-aim-to-revisit-electricity-tax-cut/live-79954869?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The Christian Democrats are in Munich, pushing to revive some tax relief that didn't make it into the budget after talks last week. And Manuela Schwesig faces a vote on a new term as regional leader. Follow DW.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Can a 'coalition of the willing' create momentum for a fossil fuel phaseout?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:451290b2e30d1d2f61fd0a6294b336c263936ff64ed640e390dbcbfe66d0c25d</id><updated>2026-11-26T08:38:13Z</updated><published>2026-11-16T08:23:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/can-a-coalition-of-the-willing-create-momentum-for-a-fossil-fuel-phaseout/a-79926748--1f05ab68dfcb.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/can-a-coalition-of-the-willing-create-momentum-for-a-fossil-fuel-phaseout/a-79926748?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">In April, about 60 countries held an unprecedented meeting in Colombia to work out a plan to slowly quit oil, coal and gas. How influential is this coalition at the COP31 climate summit?</summary><category term="Environment" /></entry><entry><title>AI in classrooms: Fighting the great 'dumbing down'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:aa7833a5524fcee963cddb881abab70db2e98852583967da096706265f4fd5eb</id><updated>2026-11-26T08:38:13Z</updated><published>2026-11-16T07:46:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/ai-in-classrooms-fighting-the-great-dumbing-down/a-79949229--354992b7f6e4.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/ai-in-classrooms-fighting-the-great-dumbing-down/a-79949229?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Research suggests that students who aren't careful about how they use ChatGPT and other AI tools risk poorer academic outcomes. It's a huge challenge for teachers.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>German economy returns to growth, so why is the country still worried?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4b5e6ff89cb0362b2a22fc2899bc5ab1665eda24c1ecded231fcb0b123fe8845</id><updated>2026-11-26T08:38:13Z</updated><published>2026-11-15T16:12:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/german-economy-returns-to-growth-so-why-is-the-country-still-worried/a-79932220--24d2aa1d0aab.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/german-economy-returns-to-growth-so-why-is-the-country-still-worried/a-79932220?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The German economy is growing again, albeit slightly. However, economists warn that without reforms, higher productivity and solid public finances, a loss of prosperity and growing debt threaten future generations.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>Despite restrictive abortion laws, Poland's 'Abortomat' — a locker that dispenses abortion pills — helps women who want to end a pregnancy</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b9dab51e130b84f738cf9f7ec580bdae7d3e844b56275f21688628401369e73c</id><updated>2026-11-26T08:38:13Z</updated><published>2026-11-15T14:40:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/polish-activists-face-opposition-as-they-make-abortion-more-accessible/a-79943914--39db4083c558.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/despite-restrictive-abortion-laws-poland-s-abortomat-a-locker-that-dispenses-abortion-pills-helps-women-who-want-to-end-a-pregnancy/a-79943914?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Abortion laws in Poland are very restrictive. Activists there have found a new way to help women wanting to terminate a pregnancy: the "Abortomat," a locker that dispenses abortion pills. But they face fierce opposition.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Germany news: Germany holds national day of remembrance</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f2d7b22f420b2ee4f2c2cb8f8897cabf926d5bba7c3ac0f8610c470c3e2f25b5</id><updated>2026-11-26T08:38:13Z</updated><published>2026-11-15T07:23:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-news-germany-holds-national-day-of-remembrance/live-79947500--7252f2ee958f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-news-germany-holds-national-day-of-remembrance/live-79947500?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Events were held for "Volkstrauertag," a day commemorating victims of war and oppression. Meanwhile, experts said the country is headed for a budget crisis.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>How AI is likely to change Germany's job market</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:38a8956039a7d668826e9d5b9cd7f911173c62f665104e0f39f5b9bd011e09c9</id><updated>2026-11-26T08:38:13Z</updated><published>2026-11-15T05:36:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/how-ai-is-likely-to-change-germany-s-job-market/a-79941597--3a5b2bd9406d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/how-ai-is-likely-to-change-germany-s-job-market/a-79941597?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The scale of the economic disruption caused by AI has led even conservative politicians to talk about universal basic income. But economists aren't convinced, and campaigners think we need to ask deeper questions.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>Ukraine: Zelenskyy says security deal could go to referendum</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:953e2e020135ee27609300e0862b0ccaaaecd95c438010e93e4d4d16970e54ef</id><updated>2026-11-26T08:38:13Z</updated><published>2026-11-14T11:40:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/ukraine-zelenskyy-says-security-deal-could-go-to-referendum/a-79947535--17ea05d7ca0f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/ukraine-zelenskyy-says-security-deal-could-go-to-referendum/a-79947535?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The US has broached the idea of Kyiv giving up the Donbas region in exchange for NATO membership, the Ukrainian president said.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Wolf Biermann at 90: The singer who defied East Germany</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f27f675382402a7f7ee5e23b0f8b2ea6c89a6957331957c005ca276f07142f05</id><updated>2026-11-26T08:38:13Z</updated><published>2026-11-14T10:00:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/wolf-biermann-at-90-the-singer-who-defied-east-germany/a-79915297--17726feda083.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/wolf-biermann-at-90-the-singer-who-defied-east-germany/a-79915297?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">His life is a reflection of contemporary German history, addressed via his songs and sharp wit. At 90, he's as feisty as ever.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>Turkey uses espionage accusations to pressure government critics</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:080df7873ba1e73818a8006dc36beae3d0cd42d8c5f9874d65124705d64e7101</id><updated>2026-11-26T08:38:13Z</updated><published>2026-11-14T07:31:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/turkey-uses-espionage-accusations-to-pressure-government-critics/a-79943768--a2686613e6a3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/turkey-uses-espionage-accusations-to-pressure-government-critics/a-79943768?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The arrest of a German foundation's employee in Istanbul this week has put the focus back on pressure tactics used by the Erdogan administration. The arrest is far from the first of its kind.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>What's going on with the polar vortex?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5df8e9492c33e874e41b811cc466bcfc41be99e0c2b6cd86d661f217e879bafd</id><updated>2026-11-26T08:38:13Z</updated><published>2026-11-13T16:34:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/what-s-going-on-with-the-polar-vortex/a-79943105--6a28f0640609.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/what-s-going-on-with-the-polar-vortex/a-79943105?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Observations show the ring of fierce winds that rotate at the Earth's North Pole has changed direction. Scientists say it's a historic disruption and the earliest reversal on record. What could it mean for the weather?</summary><category term="Environment" /></entry><entry><title>Ice hockey impasse as Russia threatens sanctions on Canada, Germany</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ebce1a353b4ce9e5a072a7fac34f977dcd8554a47f19f344bd9cd8bf03205354</id><updated>2026-11-26T08:38:13Z</updated><published>2026-11-13T16:02:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/ice-hockey-impasse-as-russia-threatens-sanctions-on-canada-germany/a-79942676--52aad908ad79.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/ice-hockey-impasse-as-russia-threatens-sanctions-on-canada-germany/a-79942676?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Two weeks after the CAS ordered ice hockey's governing body to reintegrate Russia into international play, a solution remains elusive. Now Russia has threatened to take legal action against two tournament hosts.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Germany's Nmecha won't repeat controversial goal celebration</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5f0b199cafda31aac409bfae55ac63e9fa7ff855596e4a3f57b47026cba0efba</id><updated>2026-11-26T08:38:13Z</updated><published>2026-11-13T11:04:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-s-nmecha-won-t-repeat-controversial-goal-celebration/a-79937994--cc5ab533247b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-s-nmecha-won-t-repeat-controversial-goal-celebration/a-79937994?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Germany head coach Jürgen Klopp has said midfielder Felix Nmecha will not repeat a goal celebration that sparked controversy over the past week. Germany are set to face Serbia and the Netherlands in the Nations League.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Could lack of money sink TFFF rainforest fund before it even launches?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2ce451411ab893eab8d6be053b5cd9f033a127f6f03c11977a4db7234bce757c</id><updated>2026-11-26T08:38:13Z</updated><published>2026-11-13T08:12:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/could-lack-of-money-sink-tfff-rainforest-fund-before-it-even-launches/a-79878673--227abf2cebee.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/could-lack-of-money-sink-tfff-rainforest-fund-before-it-even-launches/a-79878673?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The TFFF rainforest fund aims to make forest conservation more profitable than deforestation. But a lack of money may prevent it from getting off the ground.</summary><category term="Environment" /></entry><entry><title>Iranian activist and Nobel Peace Prize winner Narges Mohammadi shares her story in memoir</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4ab8e2b40260dffb9f5d4cc58090d68f6a67f6c8a3b16485dd16d0696a1ffb0b</id><updated>2026-11-26T08:38:13Z</updated><published>2026-11-13T08:00:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/iranian-activist-and-nobel-peace-prize-winner-narges-mohammadi-shares-her-story-in-memoir/a-79868167--a983bd7e2dcc.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/iranian-activist-and-nobel-peace-prize-winner-narges-mohammadi-shares-her-story-in-memoir/a-79868167?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Written and smuggled out of prison, the 2023 Nobel Prize laureate's memoir reveals the cost of defying Iran's regime and fighting for freedom.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>Jensen Huang: Spy row, affairs leave Nvidia without its rockstar CEO</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:abd087e8d5d781a68353847bc88b4e3cdbf97e3a57c1e990376fd88a51efcae8</id><updated>2026-11-26T08:38:13Z</updated><published>2026-11-12T15:08:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/jensen-huang-spy-row-affairs-leave-nvidia-without-its-rockstar-ceo/a-79926972--e6a7da621d57.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/jensen-huang-spy-row-affairs-leave-nvidia-without-its-rockstar-ceo/a-79926972?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Jensen Huang, who built Nvidia into the world’s dominant AI chipmaker, is stepping down as CEO over extramarital affairs. DW examines how losing its figurehead will affect the firm and the US-China AI race.</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>What are fossil fuels?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8feede44b63e3836545601dce94f72b204969414a9023570f3170c87f04e9939</id><updated>2026-11-26T08:38:13Z</updated><published>2026-11-12T12:04:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/what-are-fossil-fuels/a-67970540--1920eabf4714.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/what-are-fossil-fuels/a-67970540?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">They are in our shampoo bottles, power our cars and heat our homes. But what actually are fossil fuels, and why do they matter?</summary><category term="Climate" /></entry><entry><title>Intelligent women get less help at work, study finds</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0247ab6596a4299f7a2290f89f1588dd5507abd31df17d27d28ae87ad7e8d326</id><updated>2026-11-26T08:38:13Z</updated><published>2026-11-12T07:21:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/intelligent-women-get-less-help-at-work-study-finds/a-79910881--d3f9551f1647.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/intelligent-women-get-less-help-at-work-study-finds/a-79910881?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Women who scored high on intelligence tests were seen as more hostile by their teammates and got less help, a new study finds. High-scoring men faced no such penalty. Research explains why.</summary><category term="Science" /></entry><entry><title>Is AIIB's complaint mechanism failing affected communities?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:29ede6cd734494378a8f4c971c9f497ea709237fa3b817bd1992d64a4a31a4e0</id><updated>2026-11-26T08:38:13Z</updated><published>2026-11-11T15:12:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/is-aiib-s-complaint-mechanism-failing-affected-communities/a-79919917--1bfa788b7764.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/is-aiib-s-complaint-mechanism-failing-affected-communities/a-79919917?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The Asian Infrastructure Investment Bank has a grievance redress mechanism for people affected by projects it finances. But those seeking to file a complaint face significant hurdles. Critics say reforms are needed.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Can global leaders put their money where their mouth is on climate?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:79ae5e70dd20111ec92d71a91dc1a461f976ef52cbcaf1fc5102cc232c29df1f</id><updated>2026-11-26T08:38:13Z</updated><published>2026-11-11T14:21:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/can-global-leaders-put-their-money-where-their-mouth-is-on-climate/a-79918744--b2fe82b3dbb0.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/can-global-leaders-put-their-money-where-their-mouth-is-on-climate/a-79918744?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">World leaders warn that geopolitical divisions are distracting from the climate crisis as negotiations focus on clean energy and financing, while Iran calls for compensation for war-related environmental damage.</summary><category term="Environment" /></entry><entry><title>DW Science explainer on the default mode network: what your brain does when you aren't focusing on anything, and why it's important.</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1cd8bc2d8fdb89df65f8cf6bdf90cadfda7c218a7b38436fb33bb4d9c5c60c6e</id><updated>2026-11-26T08:38:13Z</updated><published>2026-11-11T06:57:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/dw-science-explainer-on-the-default-mode-network-what-your-brain-does-when-you-aren-t-focusing-on-an/a-79908787--cf91bcf53b1d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/dw-science-explainer-on-the-default-mode-network-what-your-brain-does-when-you-aren-t-focusing-on-anything-and-why-it-s-important/a-79908787?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Doing nothing might be the ultimate brain hack. When you're bored, the brain goes into default mode network. It's not only healthy for you, but it may also shape the very essence of your identity.</summary><category term="Science" /></entry><entry><title>Germany slips in climate protection rankings as other countries make gains</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3aba3bb788085b93e71965ea0533d98eba0ac5e42140035a4904bfd9aaca3d2a</id><updated>2026-11-26T08:38:13Z</updated><published>2026-11-11T06:41:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-slips-in-climate-protection-rankings-as-other-countries-make-gains/a-79913635--edb7d622928e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-slips-in-climate-protection-rankings-as-other-countries-make-gains/a-79913635?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Record renewable energy growth is driving climate progress in some countries, but Germany and many major emitters are falling behind.</summary><category term="Environment" /></entry><entry><title>Controversial kinship: From colonial rule to the Holocaust?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5928c786253c35dfacbdafb9ba0fd02bf1288b2b586408f4b16d8b831eb8bc61</id><updated>2026-11-26T08:38:13Z</updated><published>2026-11-10T15:49:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/controversial-kinship-from-colonial-rule-to-the-holocaust/a-79902228--16129c6452e2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/controversial-kins